2026-06-28T10:17:11.128Z [DEBUG] Tool invocation result: [{"additions":9,"base":{"ref":"release/9.0","repo":{"full_name":"jeffhandley/dotnet-runtime-servicing-release-manager"},"sha":"e78294e3b7891a40c4e0a3934015e1c0f4c0018c"},"body":"## Customer Impact\n- [x] Customer reported\n\nFixes #1 (mock). `Math.Round(double)` uses banker&#39;s rounding by default, so `Math.Round(2.5)` returns `2` instead of `3`. Customers porting from frameworks that round half away from zero get wrong totals.\\n\\n### Expected Result\\n`Math.Round(2.5)` returns `3`\\n\\n### Actual Result\\n`Math.Round(2.5)` returns `2`\\n\\n```csharp\\nSystem.Console.WriteLine(System.Math.Round(2.5)); // prints 2, expected 3\\n```\\n\\n## Regression?\\n- [ ] No\\n\\n## Risk\\nLow.","changed_files":1,"commits":1,"created_at":"2026-06-28T10:05:13Z","draft":false,"head":{"ref":"mock/math-round-fix","repo":{"full_name":"jeffhandley/dotnet-runtime-servicing-release-manager"},"sha":"ddc997cc41db75a493f242a4be5f6a10ef9f78dc"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeffhandley/dotnet-runtime-servicing-release-manager/pull/1","labels":["Servicing-approved","area-System.Runtime"],"mergeable_state":"clean","merged":false,"number":1,"state":"open","title":"[release/9.0] Fix Math.Round to round .5 midpoints away from zero","updated_at":"2026-06-28T10:05:14Z","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1031940?v=4","id":1031940,"login":"jeffhandley","profile_url":"https://github.com/jeffhandley"}}]
