      "reasoning_text": "Looking at the PR details now—it's a fix for Math.Round behavior with .5 midpoints targeting the 9.0 release branch, authored by jeffhandley and marked with servicing approval.\n\nChecking against the inclusion criteria: it has the `area-System.Runtime` label, carries the `Servicing-approved` tag, and includes a customer impact section with a bug report reference. None of the exclusion criteria apply—it's not from the maestro bot, doesn't have infrastructure labels, and isn't test-only. The PR qualifies for reproduction.\n\nThe core issue is that Math.Round(2.5) currently returns 2 using banker's rounding instead of the expected 3, which is actually the documented .NET behavior but apparently needs adjustment.\n\nI need to create a minimal repro that demonstrates Math.Round(2.5) returning 2 on the baseline SDK, then verify the bug reproduces. I'll also need to check the PR's changed files and comments to confirm it's touching the right product source code and avoid duplicating any existing repro work.",
