      "reasoning_text": "The changed file is in the product source directory, which confirms this should be included. There are no existing comments to worry about deduplication, so I'll build a repro. The base branch is from the release series and has the servicing approval, and it doesn't fall into any excluded categories.\n\nThe bug is that `Math.Round(2.5)` returns `2` instead of `3`. This is actually standard .NET behavior since `Math.Round(double)` uses banker's rounding by default, but the PR expects it to round away from zero. On the baseline .NET 9 SDK, the repro will show the actual value as `2`, confirming the bug exists.\n\nFor the repro, I need to target .NET 9.0. Since file-based apps aren't supported until .NET 10, I'll create a unit test project using xunit with a `[Fact]` that asserts `Math.Round(2.5) == 3` — this will fail on the buggy baseline, demonstrating the issue.\n\nNow I'm setting up the workspace and installing the baseline GA SDK for .NET 9. The SDK installation will take a few minutes, so I'll start that process and work through the setup step by step.",
